netcore is a native network manager for FreeBSD. A small root daemon
manages Wi-Fi association through wpa_supplicant (D-Bus or control socket),
obtains leases with dhcpcd, monitors kernel interface and address changes
through NETLINK_ROUTE, and exposes a versioned D-Bus API. netcore also ships a
command-line client, a GTK4 desktop application, and panel integrations for
XFCE, GNOME Shell and KDE Plasma.

The daemon can optionally place its Netlink parser in a Capsicum capability
mode child process.